-- title:
--   The transversal boundary set
-- statement:
--   For a natural ground size $n$, let $\mathcal S_n$ be the finite set of all subsets of the paired ground set $[n]\times\{0,1\}$. The transversal boundary is
--   $$\mathcal T_n=\{S\in\mathcal S_n:\operatorname{classifyState}(S)=\mathrm{transversal}\}.$$
--   These are the states with exactly one occupied label in each pair. The definition includes the empty ground set and supplies the boundary used by the positive-time trace analysis. This bundle defines the set only; it contains no spectral-gap estimate.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/TransversalTraceSpectralGap.lean#L21-L25

